---
import "./sternzeit.css";
---

<figure class="strip-figure" id="daylight">
    <div class="strip-panel daylight-panel" data-export="daylight">
        <svg aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The year at the chosen place, day by day from left to right, midnight to midnight from top to bottom on the chosen
        clock, its daylight saving time included: <span class="daylight-key daylight-day">day</span>, the <span class="daylight-key daylight-golden"
            >golden</span
        > and the <span class="daylight-key daylight-blue">blue</span> hour, then nautical and astronomical twilight,
        each a shade darker, and night. The line through the golden hour is sunrise and sunset. Click to move the moment
        there. Try another latitude below: the farther from the equator, the more the days swing over the year, and the
        longer the twilights last.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./daylight.js";
</script>
